  "critical": false,
  "description": "Rotary-wing aircraft generating lift and thrust from horizontally-spinning rotors. Encompasses rotor aerodynamics (articulated, semi-rigid, and rigid hubs with flapping, lagging, and feathering degrees of freedom), swashplate-based collective and cyclic control, anti-torque systems (tail rotor, Fenestron, NOTAR, coaxial), power transmission gearboxes, and autorotative emergency flight. Enables vertical takeoff and landing, hover, and low-speed maneuver flight independent of runways, supporting utility transport, aerial crane, search-and-rescue, and observation roles.",
